  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Friday)\nIssued at 937 PM CDT Fri Sep 4 2026\n\nHeat will persist through the long term as well. The vast ridge of\nhigh pressure that is centered over the Southern Plains and Mid MS\nValley will expand eastward to encompass the rest of the Southeast \nearly this week. Mid week, a trough will swing through the southern\nCanadian prairie provinces dampening the ridge, and sfc high \npressure will set up along the Appalachians. This set up could create\na CAD expanding into NE AL and portions of Southern Middle TN. If \nthis comes to fruition, adjustments to POPs (slight increase) and \ntemps (slight decrease) would be needed. Regardless, it looks like \ntemps will remain in the 90s throughout the week, which is par for \nthe course this month, but running a tad higher than seasonal norms \nwhich is 87-88 degrees. Heat index values will hover around 100 \ndegrees and the NWS Heat Risk will be a level 2 (Moderate Level) for \nthe large majority of us. Remain heat smart:\nslow down, cool down, stay hydrated and NEVER leave people or pets\nin vehicles.",
